# Cursor rules — FilsPay monorepo
# See CLAUDE.md. Key points:
# - Money is integer fils, 1 BD = 1000 fils. Never cents, never floats.
#   Parse with parseBhdToFils; rates via applyRateFils.
# - Settlement business day is Asia/Bahrain (UTC+3) midnight to midnight.
# - Money-moving code locks the row (SELECT ... FOR UPDATE) and validates under the lock.
# - Bearer secrets come from node:crypto, never Math.random.
# - Every merchant-scoped query filters by the authenticated merchant id.
# - Refunds are live: POST /v1/merchants/:merchantId/refunds (alias /v1/refunds).
# - Tests that assert a bug are fixed with the bug.
# - Do not run seed / `down -v` / reporting rebuild / tests against real data.
